      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1916-10-21_WidnesExaminer_art0021" n="art0021">
        <head>cated Teachers.</head>
        <p>cated Teachers.</p>
        <p>The following is a list of the students sif the Warrington Training College who are ".recog- nised as certificated teachers" upon the ex- amination, August, 1916. The name of a subject in patentliesis weans that the student has "passed with credit" in that subject in the ordinary course. Two Year Students.</p>
        <p>Ethel Abbott, Eveline Adams (mathematics), Dinah F. Askew (teaching, music, and mathe- matics),</p>
        <p>Rosa Ball (teaching and science), Elizabeth E. Banister (teaching); Florence M. Bankes, Eunice Barker, Elsie E. Barnes, Cecily M. Barrow, Bertha Bate, Margery A. Battersby (history), Effie Benson (history), Jane Birchall, Isabella Boucher, Jane L. R. Brandreth, Doris Brez (music), Evelyn Bridge (mathematics and science), Bessie Broome. Ellen Caddick, Laura E. Carroll (music), Lucy A. Cheetham, May Clarkson (history and geo- graphy), Ena Cooper (teaching, music, English, science), Mary Cooper, Laura M. Cotter (music), Amy E. Crooks.</p>
        <p>Jennie Dixon (science). Dorothy A. Eardley (English, advanced course), Jane Evans, Winnie Evans (history). Elsie M. Fletcher.</p>
        <p>Marion H. Garner, Edytlie M. Glover, Edith E. Greenwood (geography), Hilda M. Griffiths (distinction in history; passed with credit in teaching and hygiene).</p>
        <p>Ethel G. Hall (mathematics), Kate B. Hop- wood, Doris Horsfall, Alice Horton, Sarah A. Houghton (teaching, advanced course; history), Doris Hunt (music), Margaret D. _ Hutton (hygiene). s •</p>
        <p>Ellen Johnson, Nellie G. Johnstone, Polly Jones.</p>
        <p>Alice Kay (teaching, music and mathematics); Dorothy A. Kay.</p>
        <p>Ann Leach (history, advanced course), Verena Lees (distinction in teaching; hygiene, history, geography), Wilhelmina Leonard (history, ad- vanced course), Ernestine Livesey (teaching, hygiene; music, mathematics and science), Doris M. Locker (history, advanced course), Edith Lomax.</p>
        <p>Lilian Malley (mathematics), Beatrice E. Manifold (music), Ethel M. Mason, Maria Miller, Sarah G. Moore, Marian B. Morris. Hilda Newell (music). Clara L. Quayle. Mary G. Roberts (music), Bessie M! Robin- son (history), Maggie Robinson. Sarah A. Scattergood, Lily A. Sharpe (mathematics), Isabella- Shields, Elizabeth Sowerbutts, Alice Standring, Mary Standring. Winifred Taverner, Evelyn Townson. Priscilla Valentine.</p>
        <p>Eleanor Warburton (history, advanced course; geography), Frances H. A. Wilkinson, Grace Wilkinson (history and geography), Alice E. Wilson, Mabel Witter, Mary E. Wrench. Certificated (One Year) Students.</p>
        <p>Annie Bentley (distinction in teaching, Eng- lish and history). Frances A. Derbyshire (English and history). , Annie Duncan (teaching advanced; English and history). Annie Holmes (English and history). Margaret E. Lown (history). Ida M. Maughan (teaching, advanced course; English and history). Fanny P. Parker (hygiene and English). Ex-student. ,</p>
