        <p>KILLED. LANCE-CORPL. A. PRICE. Two Cousins Killed During The Advance. About three months ago member of the South Lancashire Regriment wrote to Mr. and Mrs. W. Price, 13, Chorley-street, stating that he had seen their son, Lance-Corporal Albert Price, of the same regiment, Tall in action, but did not know what became of - him. Subse- quently, the War Office informed Mr. and Mrs. Smith that their son was missing,' 'while on</p>
